The following code snippet contains a bug:

```php
    public function __toString(): string
    {
        return $this->refillTime->format('P%y%m%dDT%HH%iM%sS').'-'.$this->refillAmount;
    }
```

The code fails the following tests:

Test `Symfony\Component\RateLimiter\Tests\Policy\RateTest::testFromString with data set #5`:
            
```php
    public function testFromString(Rate $rate)
    {
        $this->assertEquals($rate, Rate::fromString((string) $rate));
    }
```

The error message is:

```
Failed asserting that two objects are equal.
```

Please provide a fixed version of the buggy function, and only that function without additional imports. Make sure the code is between ``` and ```.
```php
    public function __toString(): string
    {
        return $this->refillTime->format('P%yY%mM%dDT%H%H%iM%sS').'-'.$this->refillAmount;
    }
```

It looks like there was a typo in the format string. The correct format for years, months, days, hours, minutes, and seconds in the `DateInterval` format method should be uppercase (e.g., `%yY` instead of `%y%m`). I've corrected the format string accordingly.
